we all know things on euphoria can get a  little bit crazy  and that's why we can't stop watching  but things were also insane  behind the scenes one scene required the  construction of a rotating room and  another had actress zendaya reaching for  her inhaler  how would i rate you that's not the  point  of course we're excited about the second  season of euphoria  we just want to make sure our favorites  are going to be returning to the cast  thankfully we've confirmed zendaya will  be back to reprise her role as rue  bennett and the cast has gotten together  for table reads for the new scripts  this pic confirmed angus cloud will be  back and sydney sweeney announced her  return on the chicks in the office  podcast  storm reed claims that she'll be back to  reprise her role as gia  and we'd be surprised if the rest of the  main cast doesn't return for the second  season  right in the first episode of euphoria  things got spun out of control  and pulling off this tricky scene took a  lot more than building a simple set  piece  the crew actually constructed a rotating  room that zendaya walked through with  cameras following her the whole way  according to zendaya it was incredibly  disorienting  but she had it better than the  partygoers who had to be strapped  to the room while it was rotating  everything is just spinning  and you have no sense of where the real  world  is putting together a musical number may  sound simpler than having a room rotate  but the all for us scene in episode 8  was totally over the top  it took over 200 people including a  choir and marching band  and there were snare bass and tenor  drums a woodwind section  and brass instruments in play although  it was a ton of work and required  careful coordination from the  choreographer zendaya claims the energy  on set was high  and everyone was excited about the scene  and happy to be on the euphoria set  a lot of hard work went into making the  first season and the cast is already  talking about what will happen next  according to storm reed the cast knows  that we're excited about the follow-up  to the first season and all of our  questions will soon be answered  during an interview with entertainment  weekly storm confirmed that any  lingering questions will be answered in  the first couple of episodes in the  second season  while that's definitely exciting we also  assume that those episodes will also  cause us to ask  new and exciting questions about our  favorite characters  euphoria creator sam levinson believes  the right camera angles can help express  the character's emotions  so instead of filming in a static set he  makes ample use of glide cameras and  dollies to follow the stars while they  move through each scene  sam believes that this ends up making  the show feel more personal to those of  us watching at home  how do we allow our camera to articulate  it for the character  we're excited to see our favorite  euphoria characters returning for a  second season  but we're also optimistic about who  we'll be meeting next  actor kelvin harrison jr has been in  films like loose and waves  and now he's joining the cast of  euphoria apparently  kelvin wanted to be part of the first  season but could not make it work with  his busy schedule  but now he's looking forward to getting  started and says he's already enjoying  his connections to the rest of the cast  a casting call for the second season  revealed that they were looking for  someone to play darien who's an outsider  described as sensitive  vulnerable and mischievous who might not  be the coolest guy around but is one of  the more interesting ones  could this be kevin's role on the show  finding a carnival to film episode 4 was  a tough task  so the crew ended up making their own  they brought in all of the carnival  rides and equipment just two days before  the scene was filmed  obviously the crew had their work cut  out for them but the cast struggled with  this scene too  zendaya called it a nightmare and said  it was so dusty she was forced to rely  on her inhaler  sam levinson admitted that it was both  dusty and freezing cold  and it took six long days to get all of  the shots they needed to make the  episode  even though it was hard work both  zendaya and sam agreed that it was worth  it in the end  sam had the idea to create a setting  that can be  dreamy but based in reality  barbie ferreira opened up to the new  york times about her thoughts on her  character cat hernandez  she says that she's looking forward to  cat making bad decisions in season 2  and that she thinks her character is a  part of the lgbt plus community  some fans believe that barbie was  hinting cat's orientation will be a plot  point in the second season  and could influence her storyline  coming up with a script for euphoria was  not easy and neither was getting the  music  just right creator sam levinson believes  in thinking outside the box and  combining many different styles to get  the show's soundtrack  just right he described the music for  euphoria as danny elfman meets jesus  meets gospel  and that's actually the perfect  description composer labyrinth  totally understood sam's vision and made  it his mission to combine auditory and  visual effects to get the biggest impact  possible in each scene  the cast members of euphoria do a lot  more than just reading lines  they have a certain amount of input on  their characters hunter schaefer plays  jules vaughn and says she feels an  intense connection to her character  she admits that at first it was a little  awkward since transition is such a  personal experience but  she was glad to be able to portray  aspects of it that many people may not  think about  it was also a challenge to relive some  of her own memories and experiences that  were painful at the time  but overall hunter loves being a part of  the show and the fact that jules is  based on her  i don't want to have this conversation  when he was getting ready to put the  show together sam levinson made vision  boards for the characters  and actually used a photo of zendaya as  the one for roo  zandaya was flattered that sam thought  she was qualified to bring the character  to life  and is extremely proud of her work on  the series sydney sweeney likes making  interactive diaries for her characters  and yes  she has one of cassie howard but as for  how it looks like that's going to stay a  secret since sydney avoids sharing them  with even her fellow cast members  the stars of euphoria claim it's a fun  show to work on but they have to deal  with a lot of heavy themes that  can be draining according to sidney  sweeney the cast has access to an  intimacy coordinator behind the scenes  who makes sure everyone feels  comfortable during the filming process  sydney claims the coordinator helps them  speak up and works to make sure the  environment on set feels safe  for everyone euphoria has such a  talented cast that you might be  surprised by how many of them are new to  acting  barbie ferreira was nervous the casting  director wouldn't take her seriously  because of her past as a model  she worried that seeing her in person  without perfect hair and lighting would  mean missing out on the part  and says that she's grateful for  euphoria for giving her a chance to  prove herself  how she wants to be portrayed how she  wants to be viewed in the world  hunter schaefer was working as a  full-time model when she saw the casting  call and decided to try out after a  suggestion from her agent  angus cloud wasn't working as a model  but euphoria  was his first acting gig  jacob allordy's character is no stranger  to confrontation but  behind the scenes jacob ended up paying  the price for one of his fights  when nate fought with his dad jacob  admits the filming process was  physically grueling he wanted to make  things as real as possible  but maybe he got a little bit too real  jacob ended up with a concussion and  found himself throwing up after leaving  the set but  jacob managed to keep this injury from  sam levinson who was surprised to learn  about it after the fact  he clarified that there are medics stunt  coordinators and stunt doubles on set to  keep the star safe  roo's sister gia will be returning for  season 2 and according to storm reed  we'll end up seeing much more of her  this time around the first season  focused on a specific  character in each episode and storm says  it's time for gia to have her own time  to shine  she says we can look forward to seeing  her character step out of her sister's  shadow and step up as her own person  daniela davey is the head euphoria  makeup artist and she loves the fact  that sam levinson has embraced bold  bright colorful looks on the cast  apparently sam likes watching youtube  makeup tutorials as much as we do and  agreed to let her go all out  daniela claims that usually tv makeup is  designed to be consistent and  subtle but this is not the case she  tries to keep their looks consistent  with their personalities which is why  jules has such fun  imperfect and experimental looks at  first they considered having roo wear no  makeup but decided to  challenge people's perceptions of the  character by having her go bold and  sparkly when she does decide to get  dolled up  this is the first time that we really  get to see roo like genuinely happy  about life  it's clear that creator sam levinson is  all for pushing the envelope and he has  some strong ideas about where the series  is heading but a big reason the show is  so successful is because he's not afraid  to take input from the talented people  around him  according to hunter shafer sam admits  that there's only so much  a white straight man can know about the  diverse characters in euphoria  so he relies on the actors bringing  their own lives and experiences into the  script writing process  hunter says that it's a collaborative  effort and she believes that's reflected  in the nuanced characters  one area where sam does have a lot of  first-hand knowledge  he admits that in the past he struggled  with issues similar to ruse  complete with anxiety and mood swings  heightened by the teenage experience  even though there's a lot of careful  costuming going on behind the scenes of  euphoria  there are certainly plenty of scandalous  ones actor eric dane offered to bear it  all during a particularly intense scene  but the crew decided that it would be  best if he wore  a particular prosthetic part during a  scene when kat has a scandalous skype  call  she wanted to have a fake piece to look  at that way her surprised and scandalous  reaction would be completely genuine  according to barbie ferreira what we saw  on euphoria was her real reaction  and not an act  before he was cast as nate jacobs things  were not going well for jacob allordy  according to this euphoria star he was  practically homeless when he auditioned  for the show  he was completely broke when he showed  up for the casting call  and promptly forgot his lines despite  his mix-up and lack of acting experience  the casting director took a chance on  him and jacob couldn't be more grateful  working on the show has been a challenge  and there's one aspect of filming he  really struggles with  being mean to his co-star alexa demi  apparently  the two of them became close during  filming and even though he was just  acting  it wasn't easy to treat his good friend  so badly  some euphoria scenes take a ton of time  and planning to pull off  but the fight between rue and her mom  was almost completely improvised  zendaya and nika king were given just a  simple line in the script that said rue  and her mom have a fight and they were  forced to wing it from there in real  life  zendaya is a very calm person who rarely  raises her voice so this scene was a  huge challenge  this intense mother-daughter moment left  zendaya feeling light-headed and  nauseous  i was um with my mom and my uh  my little sister and we were listening  to this  this song are you looking forward to the  second season of euphoria  share your thoughts on your favorite  characters and predictions for what will  happen to them next with us  and your fellow fans in the comments  section stay connected with us here at  the things by clicking subscribe and  turning on your notifications  we'll see you next time

